<article class="glass-card rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-8 text-slate-300">
  <div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight mb-3">
      Business Quotes & Price Estimate Strategy Guide
    </h2>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      A project quote (or price estimate) sets transparent pricing expectations before starting work. Providing potential clients with a detailed, itemized quote builds credibility, prevents scope creep during execution, and establishes clear legal boundaries for project deliverables.
    </p>
  </div>

  {/* Formula Box */}
  <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 space-y-3">
    <h3 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-indigo-400">
      Quote Total Calculation Formula
    </h3>
    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-indigo-950/40 border border-indigo-500/30 text-center font-mono text-sm sm:text-base text-white font-bold">
      Estimated Total = ∑ (Estimated Hours × Hourly Rate) + Material Expenses + Contingency Buffer (10-15%)
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      Accurate business estimates break projects down into deliverables, direct labor, overhead costs, and a risk contingency buffer to absorb unexpected technical revisions.
    </p>
  </div>

  {/* Worked Numerical Example */}
  <div class="space-y-4">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">
      Worked Numerical Example: Mobile App Development Estimate
    </h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      A digital consultant prepares a formal price estimate for a client requesting an iOS and Android client portal app:
    </p>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border-collapse font-mono">
        <thead class="bg-slate-950 text-slate-200 border-b border-slate-800 uppercase text-[10px]">
          <tr>
            <th class="p-3">Deliverable / Task</th>
            <th class="p-3 text-center">Est. Hours</th>
            <th class="p-3 text-right">Rate</th>
            <th class="p-3 text-right">Subtotal</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 text-slate-300">
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 font-sans">UX Wireframing & Prototype Design</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-center">15 hrs</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-right">$90.00</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-right text-white font-bold">$1,350.00</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 font-sans">React Native Core Application Build</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-center">45 hrs</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-right">$90.00</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-right text-white font-bold">$4,050.00</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 font-sans">Third-Party Payment & Push API Setups</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-center">10 hrs</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-right">$95.00</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-right text-white font-bold">$950.00</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 space-y-1.5 text-xs">
      <div class="flex justify-between text-slate-400">
        <span>Estimated Services Subtotal:</span>
        <span class="font-mono text-slate-200 font-bold">$6,350.00</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex justify-between text-slate-400">
        <span>Estimated Sales Tax (8.5%):</span>
        <span class="font-mono text-slate-200 font-bold">$539.75</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex justify-between text-base font-extrabold text-indigo-400 border-t border-slate-800 pt-2">
        <span>Estimated Total Quote:</span>
        <span class="font-mono">$6,889.75</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* Practical Freelancer Advice */}
  <div class="space-y-3">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">
      How to Win More Contracts with Professional Quotes
    </h3>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      <li><strong>Include an Expiration Date:</strong> Quotes should remain valid for 30 days to protect your business against material cost inflation or scheduling conflicts.</li>
      <li><strong>Specify Out-of-Scope Items:</strong> Clearly list services not included (e.g., "Content copywriting and stock photo licensing fees extra").</li>
      <li><strong>Break Down Milestones:</strong> Define deposit schedules (e.g., 50% deposit upfront upon quote acceptance, 50% upon final delivery).</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  {/* Frequently Asked Questions */}
  <div class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-800">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">
      Frequently Asked Questions About Business Quotes
    </h3>
    <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">What is the difference between an estimate and a quote?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">An estimate provides an informal price range based on preliminary details, whereas a formal quote is a fixed price offer that commits you to the specified rate once accepted by the client.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">Can I convert an accepted quote into an invoice?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Yes! SimpleInvoiceTools allows you to generate PDF quotes that match your invoice layout, making it effortless to convert approved estimates directly into final billing documents.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">How long should a business quote be valid?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Most freelancers and agencies set a 14 to 30 day validity period. This ensures you can re-negotiate pricing if project requirements or calendar availability changes before the client approves.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">Is a business quote legally binding?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Once a quote is signed or accepted via email by the client, it forms a legally binding agreement under contract law. Always include clear terms regarding project scope and revision limits.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pb-1">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">Are quote details private when created on this platform?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Yes. All estimate details, pricing terms, and client names are processed 100% locally inside your browser. No data is stored on our servers.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
